  "payload": {
    "rawResponseText": "An owner converting an existing **upper-upscale hotel asset globally** should first look at the major brands that explicitly target **upper-upscale** and are known to accept conversions: **Marriott’s Autograph Collection, Sheraton, Westin, Le Méridien, Renaissance**, **Hilton’s Curio Collection, Canopy by Hilton, Hilton Hotels & Resorts, Signia by Hilton**, **IHG’s Vignette Collection, Kimpton, Voco, Crowne Plaza, Noted Collection**, **Hyatt Regency, Hyatt Centric, JdV by Hyatt, Andaz, The Standard**, and **Accor’s Pullman, Swissôtel, Mövenpick, Grand Mercure, The Sebel, Mantis, Art Series**.[10][16][2]\n\nFor a more conversion-oriented shortlist, the strongest global options from the sources are **Vignette Collection**, **Voco**, and **Noted Collection** from IHG, because IHG explicitly describes them as conversion-focused and says Noted Collection is aimed at the **upscale to upper-upscale** segment.[1][2][4] Marriott’s **Autograph Collection** and Hilton’s **Curio Collection** are also widely used soft-brand options for upper-upscale assets, and the Cornell conversion study shows historic examples of hotels converting into brands such as **Crowne Plaza, Sheraton, Westin, Hyatt, and DoubleTree**, indicating these brands have long been active conversion destinations.[10][15]\n\nIf you want the **best fit by strategy**, the choice usually breaks down like this:\n\n- **Soft-brand / independent identity preserved:** Autograph Collection, Curio Collection, Vignette Collection, JdV by Hyatt, The Unbound Collection-style positioning is often relevant, though not all of these were listed in the search results.[10][2][16]\n- **Flagship upper-upscale with broader distribution:** Sheraton, Westin, Hilton Hotels & Resorts, Hyatt Regency, Pullman, Swissôtel.[10][16]\n- **Lifestyle / design-led conversion:** Kimpton, Voco, Hotel Indigo, Canopy by Hilton, Andaz, The Standard.[2][16]\n- **Conference / business-upper-upscale:** Crowne Plaza, Renaissance, Le Méridien, Mövenpick, Grand Mercure.[2][10][16]\n\nThe most practical global owner screen is to prioritize brands that are both **upper-upscale in chain scale** and **explicitly conversion-friendly**; based on the results, that usually means **IHG, Marriott, Hilton, Hyatt, and Accor** first.[1][2][9][10][16] If you want, I can turn this into a **global conversion shortlist by region, asset type, or owner objective**.",
